  "$comment": "Cultural Delights' oven, turned as the block faces. The station hides the block while it is used and shows it here: brick walls round a cavity x 3..13, y 1..12, z 1..13 with a hearth of nether bricks, the grated door in two leaves hinged at its sides (x 3 and x 13, z 0) and swung open like gates, the baking tray (x 4..12, z 2..12, its top at y 2) sliding out between them. What bakes lies on the tray, drawn by the code: like things piled on each other, a pie's filling on its crust; the slots are the grid's places to click (row 0 at the back, column 0 on the cook's left) and move with the piles. The glow of the heat under the oven lights the inside while it is heated. While nobody uses it the block is the oven (the same models, the tray in it) and the scene draws only what lies on the tray.",
